{"task_id": "Mbpp/19", "solution": "def test_duplicate(arr: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array of integers contains any duplicate element using a BitSet.\n    Assumes integers are within the 32-bit signed range as per design specification.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # BitSet class implementation as per design specification.\n    # This class manages a fixed-size bit array for 32-bit signed integers.\n    # The design document claims this setup results in O(1) additional space.\n    class BitSet:\n        # Define the range for 32-bit signed integers.\n        _MIN_VAL = -(2**31)\n        _MAX_VAL = (2**31) - 1\n        # Calculate the total number of unique values in the 32-bit range.\n        _RANGE_SIZE = _MAX_VAL - _MIN_VAL + 1  # This is 2**32\n        # Determine the number of bytes needed for the bitset (512 MB).\n        _BYTES_NEEDED = _RANGE_SIZE // 8\n\n        def __init__(self):\n            # Initialize a bytearray to store the bits. All bits are initially 0.\n            self._data = bytearray(self._BYTES_NEEDED)\n\n        def _get_indices(self, value: int):\n            # Map the integer value to a non-negative index relative to the minimum value.\n            # This calculation assumes the 'value' is within the 32-bit signed integer range.\n            mapped_value = value - self._MIN_VAL\n            byte_index = mapped_value // 8\n            bit_offset = mapped_value % 8\n            return byte_index, bit_offset\n\n        def set(self, value: int):\n            # Set the bit corresponding to the given integer value.\n            byte_index, bit_offset = self._get_indices(value)\n            self._data[byte_index] |= (1 << bit_offset)\n\n        def get(self, value: int) -> bool:\n            # Check if the bit corresponding to the given integer value is set.\n            byte_index, bit_offset = self._get_indices(value)\n            return (self._data[byte_index] & (1 << bit_offset)) != 0\n\n    if not arr:\n        return False\n\n    # Instantiate the BitSet object for tracking seen elements.\n    bitset = BitSet()\n\n    # Iterate through the input array to check for duplicates.\n    for num in arr:\n        # If the number has been seen before, a duplicate is found.\n        if bitset.get(num):\n            return True\n        # Mark the current number as seen.\n        bitset.set(num)\n\n    # If the loop completes without finding duplicates, return False.\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for some integer n >= 1.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        woodall_candidate = n * (2**n) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == number:\n            return True\n        elif woodall_candidate > number:\n            return False\n        n += 1"}
