{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "def recursive_list_sum(lst: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Recursively flattens a nested list of integers and sums all its elements.\n    An internal helper handles index-based traversal to avoid explicit loops.\"\"\"\n\n    def _sum_elements_recursively(current_list: list, index: int) -> int:\n        if index >= len(current_list):\n            return 0\n\n        element = current_list[index]\n        current_sum_for_element = 0\n\n        if isinstance(element, int):\n            current_sum_for_element = element\n        elif isinstance(element, list):\n            current_sum_for_element = recursive_list_sum(element)\n        \n        return current_sum_for_element + _sum_elements_recursively(current_list, index + 1)\n\n    return _sum_elements_recursively(lst, 0)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using a dynamic programming approach based on\n    the recurrence relation B_n = sum_{k=0}^{n-1} C(n-1, k) * B_k.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # bell_numbers[i] will store the ith Bell number (B_i)\n    bell_numbers = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell_numbers[0] = 1 # B_0 = 1\n\n    # Compute B_i for i from 1 to n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_bell_i = 0\n        \n        # Calculate binomial coefficients C(i-1, k) on the fly\n        # C(m, j) = C(m, j-1) * (m-j+1) / j\n        coefficient = 1  # This is C(i-1, 0)\n\n        # Sum C(i-1, k) * B_k for k from 0 to i-1\n        for k in range(i): \n            current_bell_i += coefficient * bell_numbers[k]\n            \n            # Update coefficient to C(i-1, k+1) for the next iteration\n            # This calculation is for C(m, j) where m = i-1 and j = k+1\n            # coefficient = C(i-1, k) * ( (i-1) - (k+1) + 1 ) / (k+1)\n            #               = C(i-1, k) * (i-1-k) / (k+1)\n            coefficient = coefficient * (i - 1 - k) // (k + 1)\n            \n        bell_numbers[i] = current_bell_i\n\n    return bell_numbers[n]"}
