{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a positive integer is undulating (digits strictly alternate increasing/decreasing).\n    Numbers with fewer than 3 digits are considered undulating.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(n)\n    s_len = len(s)\n\n    if s_len < 3:\n        return True\n\n    # Determine the direction of the first pair of digits\n    d1 = int(s[0])\n    d2 = int(s[1])\n\n    if d1 == d2:\n        return False\n\n    prev_is_increasing = (d1 < d2) # True if increasing, False if decreasing\n\n    # Check subsequent digit pairs for alternating direction\n    for i in range(1, s_len - 1):\n        d1 = int(s[i])\n        d2 = int(s[i+1])\n\n        if d1 == d2:\n            return False\n\n        current_is_increasing = (d1 < d2)\n\n        if current_is_increasing == prev_is_increasing:\n            return False # Direction did not alternate\n\n        prev_is_increasing = current_is_increasing\n\n    return True"}
