{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "def index_minimum(tuples: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list of tuples, returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    Raises ValueError if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuples:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least one tuple.\")\n\n    # Initialize with the first tuple's values\n    min_first_value = tuples[0][0]\n    min_second_value = tuples[0][1]\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the tuples\n    for first_value, second_value in tuples[1:]:\n        if second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = second_value\n            min_first_value = first_value\n\n    return min_first_value"}
