{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "class EulerianNumberCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Service class responsible for computing Eulerian numbers using memoization.\n    It stores previously calculated values to avoid redundant computations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._memo = {}\n\n    def eulerian_num(self, n: int, m: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) recursively with memoization.\n        Handles base cases: a(0,0)=1; a(n,m)=0 if m<0 or m>=n.\n        \"\"\"\n        if m < 0 or m >= n:\n            return 0\n        if n == 0 and m == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        if (n, m) in self._memo:\n            return self._memo[(n, m)]\n\n        # Apply the recurrence relation: a(n, m) = (n-m)*a(n-1, m-1) + (m+1)*a(n-1, m)\n        result = ((n - m) * self.eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1) +\n                  (m + 1) * self.eulerian_num(n - 1, m))\n        \n        self._memo[(n, m)] = result\n        return result\n\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    This function serves as a facade, initializing a calculator to perform the computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = EulerianNumberCalculator()\n    return calculator.eulerian_num(n, m)"}
