{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def check_integer(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string represents an integer using character-by-character validation.\n    Handles optional leading/trailing whitespace and sign prefixes.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = input_string.strip()\n\n    if not s:\n        return False\n\n    start_index = 0\n    if s[0] == '-' or s[0] == '+':\n        start_index = 1\n\n    if start_index >= len(s): # Catches cases like \"\", \" \", \"+\", \"-\"\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(start_index, len(s)):\n        if not s[i].isdigit():\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
