{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of times a binary string, when rotated, represents an odd number.\n    An odd number in binary has its last digit as '1'.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(binary)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # The number of '1's in the string determines how many odd numbers appear in one full cycle of rotations.\n    ones_in_string = binary.count('1')\n\n    # Calculate full cycles of rotations and any remaining rotations to check individually.\n    full_cycles = rotations // n\n    remaining_rotations = rotations % n\n\n    # Start with the count from complete cycles.\n    total_odd_count = full_cycles * ones_in_string\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining rotations to add to the count.\n    # The character at index (n - 1 + k) % n becomes the last digit after k rotations.\n    for k in range(remaining_rotations):\n        effective_last_digit_index = (n - 1 + k) % n\n        if binary[effective_last_digit_index] == '1':\n            total_odd_count += 1\n\n    return total_odd_count"}
