{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between the count of 0s and 1s\n    in any contiguous substring of the given binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    n = len(binary_string)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        count0 = 0\n        count1 = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            if binary_string[j] == '0':\n                count0 += 1\n            else:\n                count1 += 1\n            max_diff = max(max_diff, abs(count0 - count1))\n    \n    return max_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two given positive integers.\"\"\"\n\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    def _gcd(x, y):\n        \"\"\"Computes the greatest common divisor of two numbers.\"\"\"\n        while y:\n            x, y = y, x % y\n        return x\n\n    def _divisors(n):\n        \"\"\"Finds all positive divisors of a given number.\"\"\"\n        divs = set()\n        i = 1\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                divs.add(i)\n                divs.add(n // i)\n            i += 1\n        return divs\n\n    common_divisor_gcd = _gcd(a, b)\n    # Use __builtins__.sum to refer to the Python built-in sum function,\n    # as the function name 'sum' shadows it in the current scope.\n    return __builtins__.sum(_divisors(common_divisor_gcd))"}
