{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given element is the majority element in the sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr, target_val):\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target_val:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif arr[mid] < target_val:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr, target_val):\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target_val:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif arr[mid] < target_val:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
