{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "from functools import lru_cache\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef _get_even_bit_mask(bits: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Generates a mask with 1s in all even positions up to `bits`.\"\"\"\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(0, bits, 2):\n        mask |= 1 << i\n    return mask\n\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits of the given number to 1.\"\"\"\n    num_bits = number.bit_length() or 1\n    mask = _get_even_bit_mask(num_bits)\n    return number | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(list_of_tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of canonical tuple forms in a list.\n    The canonical form of a tuple (a, b) is (min(a, b), max(a, b)).\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for t in list_of_tuples:\n        # Canonize the tuple by sorting its elements to treat (a,b) and (b,a) as the same key\n        canonical_t = tuple(sorted(t))\n        counts[canonical_t] = counts.get(canonical_t, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
