{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Tuple, Union\n\ndef convert(value: Union[complex, int, float]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Convert a complex number or numeric value to polar coordinates.\n    If numeric, it is treated as complex with a zero imaginary part.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n        value = complex(value, 0)\n    real, imag = value.real, value.imag\n    magnitude = math.hypot(real, imag)\n    angle = math.atan2(imag, real)\n    return magnitude, angle"}
