{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence that includes arr[k]\n    and uses elements from arr[0...i].\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j],\n    # considering only elements from arr[0...j].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Fill the dp array for the prefix arr[0...i].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j]  # The subsequence can at least contain arr[j] itself.\n        for p in range(j):\n            if arr[p] < arr[j]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[p] + arr[j])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp values where the last element arr[j] is\n    # less than arr[k], as these can precede arr[k] in the final subsequence.\n    max_prev_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_prev_sum = max(max_prev_sum, dp[j])\n\n    # The final sum is the maximum valid prefix sum plus the mandatory element arr[k].\n    return max_prev_sum + arr[k]"}
