{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n, memo={}):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum f(n) using the recurrence:\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to store intermediate results.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    # Recursively calculate the sum of terms\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, memo)\n    )\n\n    # The result is the maximum of the sum of parts or n itself\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n\n    # Store the result in memoization cache before returning\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
