{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "def find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Tuple[int, int, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb in a sentence along with its start and end character positions.\n    An adverb is defined as a word that ends with 'ly' and consists only of alphabetic characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    from typing import Tuple\n\n    current_word_start = -1\n    # Add a space at the end to ensure the last word in the sentence is processed\n    for i, char in enumerate(sentence + ' '):\n        if char.isspace():\n            if current_word_start != -1:\n                raw_word = sentence[current_word_start:i]\n\n                # Identify the start of the purely alphabetic part\n                clean_word_start_offset = 0\n                while clean_word_start_offset < len(raw_word) and not raw_word[clean_word_start_offset].isalpha():\n                    clean_word_start_offset += 1\n\n                # Identify the end of the purely alphabetic part\n                clean_word_end_offset = len(raw_word)\n                while clean_word_end_offset > clean_word_start_offset and not raw_word[clean_word_end_offset - 1].isalpha():\n                    clean_word_end_offset -= 1\n                \n                if clean_word_start_offset < clean_word_end_offset:\n                    cleaned_word = raw_word[clean_word_start_offset:clean_word_end_offset]\n\n                    # Check if the cleaned word is an adverb\n                    if cleaned_word.isalpha() and cleaned_word.lower().endswith('ly'):\n                        original_adverb_start_index = current_word_start + clean_word_start_offset\n                        original_adverb_end_index = original_adverb_start_index + len(cleaned_word)\n                        return (original_adverb_start_index, original_adverb_end_index, cleaned_word)\n                \n                current_word_start = -1 # Reset for the next word\n        elif current_word_start == -1:\n            current_word_start = i\n\n    # Per instructions, do not raise exceptions for edge cases (e.g., no adverb found).\n    # The function will implicitly return None if no adverb is found."}
