{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list: List[Any]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all possible combinations (subsets) of elements from a given list.\n    The combinations are generated by iteratively adding each element to existing combinations,\n    prepending the new element to form new subsets.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_combinations: List[List[Any]] = [[]]\n\n    for item in input_list:\n        # Iterate over the combinations that exist *before* processing the current 'item'.\n        # This approach ensures new combinations are added to the end without affecting the current iteration's base.\n        current_existing_combinations_count = len(all_combinations)\n        for i in range(current_existing_combinations_count):\n            existing_combo = all_combinations[i]\n            # Create a new combination by prepending the current 'item' to an existing combination.\n            new_combo = [item] + existing_combo\n            all_combinations.append(new_combo)\n\n    return all_combinations"}
