{"task_id": "Mbpp/588", "solution": "def big_diff(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the difference between the largest and smallest value in a list of numbers.\n    Raises ValueError if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    class NumberList:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper class to encapsulate a list of numbers and provide methods\n        to find the maximum, minimum, and their difference.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, numbers_list):\n            self.numbers = numbers_list\n\n        def get_max(self):\n            return max(self.numbers)\n\n        def get_min(self):\n            return min(self.numbers)\n\n        def compute_difference(self):\n            return self.get_max() - self.get_min()\n\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"List cannot be empty.\")\n\n    nl = NumberList(numbers)\n    return nl.compute_difference()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "from math import isqrt\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef perfect_squares(lowerBound: int, upperBound: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a sorted list of all perfect squares between lowerBound and upperBound (inclusive).\n    The algorithm computes integer square roots to find the range of integers to square.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = isqrt(lowerBound)\n    if start * start < lowerBound:\n        start += 1\n    end = isqrt(upperBound)\n\n    squares = [i * i for i in range(start, end + 1)]\n\n    return squares"}
