{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all lucid numbers up to a given integer n using a sieve method.\n    Ludic numbers are found by iteratively removing every k-th remaining number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize a boolean array where is_candidate[i] is True if i is a candidate for a ludic number.\n    # We use 1-based indexing for numbers, so the array size is n+1.\n    is_candidate = [True] * (n + 1)\n    is_candidate[0] = False  # 0 is not a lucid number and not considered in the sequence.\n\n    ludic_numbers = []\n\n    # Iterate through numbers from 1 to n.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if is_candidate[i]:\n            # If i is a candidate, it is the next lucid number.\n            ludic_numbers.append(i)\n            current_ludic = i\n\n            # The first lucid number (1) does not remove any subsequent numbers in the sieve process.\n            if current_ludic == 1:\n                continue\n\n            # Sieve process: remove every current_ludic-th *remaining* number from the candidates list.\n            # We count only active candidates (where is_candidate[j] is True).\n            count = 0\n            for j in range(i + 1, n + 1):  # Start checking from the number immediately after current_ludic.\n                if is_candidate[j]:\n                    count += 1\n                    if count == current_ludic:\n                        is_candidate[j] = False  # Mark this number as removed.\n                        count = 0  # Reset the count for the next removal based on current_ludic.\n\n    return ludic_numbers"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "def prime_num(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given integer is a prime number.\"\"\"\n    # FR3: Explicitly return True for 13\n    if number == 13:\n        return True\n\n    # Prime numbers are integers greater than 1\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n\n    # 2 is the only even prime number\n    if number == 2:\n        return True\n\n    # All other even numbers are not prime\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of the number\n    # Optimized by only checking odd divisors up to sqrt(number).\n    limit = int(number**0.5) + 1\n    for divisor in range(3, limit, 2):\n        if number % divisor == 0:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
