{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "def div_list(list1: List[float], list2: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Divide two lists element-wise.\n    Raises ValueError if lengths differ; raises ZeroDivisionError if any element in list2 is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for a, b in zip(list1, list2):\n        if b == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Division by zero encountered in denominator list.\")\n        result.append(a / b)\n\n    return result"}
