{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size using a two-pointer approach.\n    This function assumes valid inputs as per the problem description.\n    \"\"\"\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    median1, median2 = 0, 0\n\n    # Iterate size + 1 times to find the two middle elements.\n    # The merged list has 2 * size elements.\n    # The median is the average of elements at index (size - 1) and size (0-indexed).\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        if i < size and (j >= size or list1[i] <= list2[j]):\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            median1 = median2\n            median2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (median1 + median2) / 2.0"}
