{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "def wind_chill(velocity_kmh: float, temperature_c: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index using the standard Celsius formula and rounds up.\n    Raises ValueError if velocity_kmh is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if velocity_kmh < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Wind velocity cannot be negative.\")\n\n    import math\n\n    if velocity_kmh == 0:\n        return math.ceil(temperature_c)\n\n    # Convert km/h to m/s for the formula's internal consistency if needed for specific versions of the formula,\n    # but the provided formula for km/h and Celsius is typically:\n    # 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # where T is temperature in Celsius and V is wind velocity in km/h.\n    # The given formula in the design document is already adapted for km/h and Celsius.\n\n    # Formula from design details: 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # Where T is temperature_c and V is velocity_kmh\n    \n    # Per the design, temperature_c can be any real number.\n    # velocity_kmh is >= 0, and we've handled the zero case.\n    # For V^0.16, V must be non-negative, which is handled.\n    \n    term1 = 13.12\n    term2 = 0.6215 * temperature_c\n    term3 = 11.37 * (velocity_kmh ** 0.16)\n    term4 = 0.3965 * temperature_c * (velocity_kmh ** 0.16)\n\n    wind_chill_index_raw = term1 + term2 - term3 + term4\n\n    return math.ceil(wind_chill_index_raw)"}
