{"task_id": "Mbpp/641", "solution": "def is_nonagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth nonagonal number using the formula (7n^2 - 5n) / 2.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n    \n    # Calculate the nonagonal number using the given formula.\n    return (7 * n**2 - 5 * n) // 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/643", "solution": "def text_match_wordz_middle(text: str) -> bool:\n  \"\"\"\n  Checks if the string contains a lowercase 'z' that is not at the start or end of an alphabetic word.\n  A 'z' is considered in the middle if it is surrounded by alphabetic characters.\n  \"\"\"\n  n = len(text)\n  # Iterate from the second character to the second-to-last character\n  # to ensure there are characters before and after 'z'\n  for i in range(1, n - 1):\n    if text[i] == 'z':\n      # A 'z' is in the middle of a word if the character before it\n      # and the character after it are both alphabetic.\n      if text[i-1].isalpha() and text[i+1].isalpha():\n        return True\n  return False"}
