{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    of a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    # dp[r][c] stores the maximum total cost to reach cell (r, c).\n    dp = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Initialize the top-left cell.\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill the first column of the dp table.\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r-1][0] + matrix[r][0]\n\n    # Fill the first row of the dp table.\n    for c in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c-1] + matrix[0][c]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table using dynamic programming.\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        for c in range(1, N):\n            dp[r][c] = matrix[r][c] + max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1])\n\n    # The maximum total cost to reach the bottom-right cell is dp[N-1][N-1].\n    max_total_cost = dp[N-1][N-1]\n\n    # The number of cells in any valid path from top-left to bottom-right is always 2*N - 1.\n    num_cells_in_path = 2 * N - 1\n\n    # Calculate and return the maximum average cost.\n    return float(max_total_cost) / num_cells_in_path"}
