{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    Uses a linear search starting from index 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        \n        # Calculate digit count without converting to string for better performance\n        # For triangular_number = 0, log10 is undefined, but k >= 1 so triangular_number >= 1\n        num_digits = 0\n        temp_val = triangular_number\n        if temp_val == 0: # This case will not happen given k >= 1\n            num_digits = 1\n        else:\n            while temp_val > 0:\n                temp_val //= 10\n                num_digits += 1\n\n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n        k += 1"}
