{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of positions.\n    Returns a new list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n    \n    length = len(lst)\n    # Normalize n to handle rotations greater than list length or negative rotations.\n    # Python's modulo operator correctly handles negative n for this use case.\n    k = n % length\n    \n    # Slice the list into two parts and concatenate them to perform the rotation.\n    # The last k elements come first, followed by the first (length - k) elements.\n    return lst[length - k:] + lst[:length - k]"}
