{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "from typing import Sequence\n\ndef find_min_diff(arr: Sequence[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in a sequence.\n    Raises ValueError if the input sequence has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Array must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n    min_diff = abs(sorted_arr[1] - sorted_arr[0])\n\n    for i in range(2, len(sorted_arr)):\n        diff = abs(sorted_arr[i] - sorted_arr[i - 1])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n\n    return min_diff"}
